/awaab-ishak-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Awaab Ishak: Prevention of future deaths report","date":"2022-11-16","coroner":"Joanne Kearsley","area":"Manchester North","ref":"2022-0365","categories":["Child Death (from 2015)","Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-and-Department-.pdf","filename":"2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-and-Department-.pdf","promises":[{"id":629,"quote":"We are reviewing the 3.4extent to which the current DHS is the right ask of the social housing sector today; to consider the case for change; and to assess the strategic, economic and management case for different criteria. Part","summary":"Review DHS to address damp and mould concerns","timescale":"Autumn 2021"},{"id":630,"quote":"current review of the housing health and safety rating system (\"HHSRS\") will support a better understanding of the known risks of damp and mould to health.","summary":"Review HHSRS for damp and mould risk assessment","timescale":"2022"},{"id":631,"quote":"we will table an amendment to the Social Housing Regulation Bill relating to hazards in social homes.","summary":"Amend Social Housing Regulation Bill for hazard management","timescale":"subject to further discussion"},{"id":632,"quote":"I intend to direct the Regulator of Social Housing to implement the approach set out in this new policy statement in its standards.","summary":"Direct RSSH to implement policy on hazard timelines","timescale":"within six months of Royal Assent"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-letter-to-All-P.pdf","filename":"2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-letter-to-All-P.pdf","promises":[{"id":373,"quote":"The Regulator of Social Housing will be writing to you imminently on this and you should respond promptly.","summary":"Regulator to write to providers about damp and mould assessments","timescale":"imminently"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-letter-to-Legal.pdf","filename":"2022-0365-Response-from-Secretary-of-State-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities-letter-to-Legal.pdf","promises":[{"id":617,"quote":"From 1 October 2022, changes introduced by the Building Safety Act, mean that residents will no longer have to refer their complaint to a designated person, such as an MP, or wait eight weeks before the Ombudsman can consider their complaint.","summary":"Direct residents to Social Housing Ombudsman for complaints","timescale":"1 October 2022"}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/brian-harfield-prevention-of-future-deaths-report/","title":"Brian Harfield: Prevention of future deaths report","date":"2023-03-16","coroner":"Penelope Schofield","area":"West Sussex","ref":"2023-0092","categories":["Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/2023-0092-Response-from-Department-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities.pdf","filename":"2023-0092-Response-from-Department-for-Levelling-Up-Housing-and-Communities.pdf","promises":[{"id":1882,"quote":"The Government recognises that further evidence is required on the benefit of sprinklers and other additional fire protection measures in specialised housing and, to this end, we have a dedicated research workstream in place. I will consider future research findings in light of your concerns and the evidence heard at Mr [name redacted] inquest, so that we can consider what changes are necessary to reduce the risk of similar incidents in the future.","summary":"Research on sprinklers in specialised housing underway","timescale":null}]